@startuml resolve-turn-activity
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml

skinparam defaultTextAlignment left

title StarChess Core · ""resolveTurn"" — physical C guard before classification

start
:consumeNativeClassicalDoubles deletes any submit-owned\nbinding on this exact input; ordinary direct input has none;
:Read placement once into start; plansOf copies scalar\ncoordinates, promotion and extra-step fields before callbacks;
:guard both live same-side actors with isScMoveShape\nor the matched native Marine-double entitlement;
if (either live C actor has an impossible shape?) then (yes)
  :throw ScValidateError / SC_BASELINE_FEN;\nno recorder board, query, visibility callback or C effect;
  stop
endif
note right
  Captured plan scalars preserve the checked
  coordinates through later visibility callbacks.
  Changing a caller's plan cannot redirect
  an already checked native move.
end note
note right
  Missing or foreign actors still drop.
  Caller extra-step fields grant no witness.
end note
:clamp ccLives and create phase buckets;
:Buckets for this pass:\n""attacks"" · ""moveCollisions"" · ""occupy"" · ""quiets""\n""pathRevealPending"" · ""deadSquares"";
:Optional ""ProvenanceRecorder"": bind actual native carriers\nand source sequences; preserve mine occurrence order;
note right
  Actual carriers / mutation sites
  No square-continuity identity inference
end note

partition "Classify — an ordered rule list, first match wins" {
  :build ""PlanContext"" once: actor · target · ""visible0"" · ""leaps"" ·\nsieged flags · a **memoised** ""scanRay"";
  :evaluate ""RULES"" in order — first non-null outcome wins;
  note right
    Ordered classification exposes control flow
    that was implicit in scattered branches.
    Each rule returns its first matching outcome,
    so precedence remains explicit at the rule site.
  end note

  if (1 — jumpImmunity?) then (matches)
    :enemy BattleShip at ""to"" is in ""ignoreAttacksOn""\n→ drop; a jumping BattleShip is untouchable;
  elseif (2 — marineFrontStep?) then (matches)
    :same-file Marine walk meets its first occupant\n→ truncate to the last empty tile or drop;\nno capture or discovery, regardless of fog;\na blocked last-rank step cannot promote;
  elseif (3 — enemyCCSquare?) then (matches)
    :enemy CC on ""to"" → no deferred HP here;\nturn-open checks own direct CC damage;\nnon-CC enemy blocker → capture / collision / approach\naccording to start and path visibility;\nally / CC blocker / clear ray → drop, never occupy CC;
  elseif (4 — allyOccupied?) then (matches)
    :own unit on ""to"" → drop;
  elseif (5 — marineDiagonalEmpty?) then (matches)
    :empty Marine diagonal → drop unless a visible\nhostile mine supplies the capture-only target;
  elseif (6 — midPathPrecedence?) then (matches)
    :enemy aim with an intermediate ray contact\n→ resolve that contact before the further target;\n""Re1→e8"" with ""pe7"" and ""re8"" takes ""pe7"";\nally → quiet truncation; CC → later classification;
  elseif (7 — targetOnDestination?) then (matches)
    :enemy on ""to"" → visible capture / path discovery\napproach / unrevealed move collision;\nunrevealed siege contact drops instead of relocating;
  elseif (8 — minedEmptyDestination?) then (matches)
    :empty mined ""to"" + visible + reachable +\n""attacksOwnDest"" → clear the mine;\nsieged Tank fires in place, others occupy;\notherwise quiet intent defers to movement;
    :CC contact is attack/move and clears the mine;\nits adjacent destination is visible and it leaps,\nso it cannot fall through to a quiet mine arrival;
  elseif (9 — slideIntoFog?) then (matches)
    :sliding empty aim finds its first enemy ray contact\n→ visible capture / path discovery / fog collision;\nCC contact → discovery chip or stop short;
  elseif (10 — siegedEmptyShelling?) then (matches)
    :visible empty cross target with a clear ray\n→ victimless shelling, no death or relocation;\nally / CC blocker → drop; fog → quiet without relocation;
  else (11 — quietFallthrough)
    :no earlier rule claims the plan → quiet;
  endif

  :""applyOutcome"" alone writes phase buckets:\n""drop"" · ""quiet"" · ""occupy"" · ""capture(fogged?)""\n""mineClear"" · ""shelling"" · ""approach"";
  note right
    Typed outcomes prevent duplicate capture
    accounting across the native phase lists.
    Visibility assigns a target to attacks or
    movement collisions, instead of reporting
    the same victim in both destinations.
  end note

  :preserve complete plan fields when overriding ""to"";\ntruncate or drop a blocked forward step;
  note right
    Preserve full plans when a landing changes,
    so promotion metadata survives truncation.
    Coordinate reconstruction once produced
    asymmetric last-rank captures.
  end note

  :path discovery requires a fogged start target\nand positive intermediate ""pathRevealSteps"";
  :record actual query inputs and evaluated prefix privately;\ncarry query ordinal through the selected deferred branch;\nvirtual mover patches create no frame or observation image;
  note right
    Path evaluation excludes the starting square.
    Fog discovery also requires an initially
    unobserved destination, so an aim already
    in view cannot become a deferred approach.
  end note

  note right
    Defer a fogged victim with a departing plan,
    rather than booking an immediate destruction.
    The later landing respects actual departure,
    instead of retaining the original board's ghost.
  end note
}

partition "Phase 1 — attack" {
  :record the entire C attack-removal wave atomically;\nall victims share one live causal preimage;\nremove ""deadSquares"" → **afterAttack** snapshot;
}

partition "Phase 2 — move (""moveWave"": plan every landing, then time them)" {
  :skip movers that died in phase 1, and sieged rooks (never relocate);
  :""planLanding"" — every mover plans against the **same** pre-wave board,
so plan order (white first) can never decide an outcome. Quiet slides
truncate on the first **stationary** blocker — enemy blocker is captured,
ally / king blocker stops the slide one square short;
  :two opposite-colour landings → ""moverContact(timedMover(a), timedMover(b))""
(""move-timing.puml"": Hoverbike 1 tick / square, everything else 2,
leapers hold only their landing, sliders every ray square,
a mover a mine takes on landing holds nothing afterwards);
  if (contact at X?) then (yes)
    if (a Command Center in the pair?) then (yes)
      :CC reached X **first** → CC lands, the other stops one ray
square short (a leaper stays home) · CC arrived on or after the
other → CC **takes** it (""moveCollisions"" capture, occupies,
clears the mine on X) · CC vs CC → neither moves;
    else (no)
      :**both die on X**, mines untouched, no cue — whether the other
was parked there, arrived the same tick, or they passed head-on
mid-edge (reported on the lower-named square);
    endif
  else (no)
    :``land`` each mover as planned;
  endif
  :``land``: destination still held by an enemy → capture + occupy, **unless**\nanother mover already landed there (""destinationsWritten"", phase 3 only)\n→ **both die**, tile empty, no cue;
  :record actual victim retirement / mine clearing / relocation\nas one frame, including Command Center captures;
  :""mineContact"" over ""[extraStepFrom?, …pathContactSquares, dest]""
(mode **walk**) — one ordered scan answers chase **and** walk-over.
A plan carrying ""extraStepTo"" **stands down**: its landing is one hop
further, so the phase-4 arrival owns the contact list
(""mine-contact.puml"" · one walk per marine);
  :land the mover, stamp ""destinationsWritten"", defer promotion;
  :arrival mine mutation gets a distinct landed-live frame;\nretire every actual mine occurrence removed by the square filter;
  :""detonated"" → blast at the landing tile, mover dies, no promotion\nand no occupy left behind; ""chaseFrom"" set when the mine was woken\nmid-path (the first mine touched wins);
  :→ **afterMove** snapshot;
}

partition "Phase 3 — fog approaches" {
  :fizzle gates (in order): sieged origin · origin re-occupied by a\nphase-2 mover · attacker no longer on ""pathRevealFrom"" ·\n""to"" no longer holds the exact discovered victim;\nUI replay shares ""applyPathRevealAttack"" /\n""applyPathRevealCCShot"" board-state checks;
  note right
    Shared applications check the live actor
    and victim before applying a deferred attack.
    Native execution still owns exclusions and
    mine contact, rather than deriving those
    effects from a replay animation.
  end note
  :fired → ""pathRevealAttacks"" (the only mid-resolve king HP chip);
  :commit capture + relocation or CC damage + relocation atomically;\nrecord one associated acting-side consumed-target proof;
  note right
    Successful consumed target only
    No prefix / incidental observation authority
  end note
  :the approach **walked** its ray — ""mineContact"" over that walk takes\nthe mover on its landing tile → ""pathRevealMineTriggers"".\nThe shot already fired, so capture / HP chip stand;
}

partition "Delayed landings — fogged aims and skipped approaches" {
  :sync ""mines"" to the phase-3 epoch, order the pair so a plan\nlanding on the other's origin runs second (mutual swap lands both);
  :skip fired approaches (""firedFrom""), dead or moved actors,\nand destinations a phase-3 actor now owns (fizzle);
  :clear a departed ghost from the working board;
  if (live reciprocal pair selected?) then (yes)
    :swap both actors and resolve destination mine contacts;
    :record both moves atomically, then actual mine deaths;\nscratch synchronization adds no duplicate lifecycle effect;
    :copy resulting placement and remaining ""mines""\ninto ""phase3"" → **afterAll** retains removals;
    note right
      Copy surviving mines with the new placement,
      so final output retains spent-mine removals.
      Native synchronization preserves survivor
      order and duplicate occurrences.
    end note
  else (no)
    :""relocate"" with occupy trust — victim still home means\na single move-phase collision, never a second kill;
    :mirror the landing onto the phase-3 snapshot (move / blast /\ncollision, ""chaseFrom""-aware mine filter) → **afterMove** snapshot;
  endif
}

partition "Phase 4 — promotion" {
  :pawns that survived every phase promote on the ""afterAll"" board;
  :record the actual live same-side lineage transformation;
}
:return the four lists + the three snapshots;
note right
  Pending shots validate occupancy and target
  identity, not the shooter's remaining HP.
  Retaliation within the same pass preserves
  mutual draws despite ordering at zero HP.
end note
stop
@enduml
